=20
{tu'o} is not misleading, as if often is in these cases) would be what?  3x=
,=20
4x, 5x?  Clearly not what is wanted.  What is wanted is {li ce'u pi'i ceu}=
=20
for a suitable range of both=20
{ce'u}.  In short what is wanted in 1-3 is something that gives a number, n=
ot=20
a sentence as all {du'u} do eventually.
As for 4 and 5, of course functions are not necessarily involved, any more=
=20
than properties and indirect questions are in other versions of this same=20
sort of thing.  They all come down to case of identity/equivalence or their=
=20
denial and so involve only fully specified sentences .  But if we are to=20
allow one kind of abbreviation (actually it often ends up longer than the=20
original), why not all the others that come under the same rules?

